  "tagline": "Google Cloud's managed in-memory family: Valkey, Redis, Redis Cluster and Memcached.",
  "description": "Memorystore is Google Cloud's umbrella for managed caches: Memorystore for Valkey (Google's lead engine, with 9.0 as default and 9.1 in preview), Memorystore for Redis Cluster, the older single-node/standard Memorystore for Redis, and Memorystore for Memcached. The Valkey and Redis Cluster products offer zero-downtime scaling, Private Service Connect networking, persistence (RDB/AOF) and up to 99.99% SLA, and Valkey adds vector search. It is the default choice for GKE and Cloud Run apps that need a cache; cross-region options are limited to replicas and DR.",
